PACK door_fieldvm 1
IMPORT boot 1
IMPORT door 1
VIRTUAL FieldVm
VIRTUAL FvDir
VIRTUAL FvFile
-- THE BROWSER VM'S START AS A DOOR ROUTE (#1143, swap step 3): GET /ui/fieldvm (the page's `fieldvm.js connect()`: the snapshot, then the event stream).
-- The page runs its own field engine (WebAssembly, the same VM) and follows the seat's: it starts from this snapshot, {packs: {name: c1f text}, entities:
-- [{eid, cls, props}]}, and the packs that import `dom` run in the page and draw there (the About window is one: packs/about.c1f).
-- BUILT: `packs` = every pack FILE of the apps' folders whose text has the line `IMPORT dom ...` (the released seat sent every pack it loaded; the others
-- are the seat's, not the page's), by file name without `.c1f`, the text whole. They are read ONCE at boot (`FieldVm:seat`, from `Boot:seat.app_dirs`:
-- each folder is listed, each pack file read), so a request waits only for the first read; a file pack changed afterwards is not re-read (a restart does).
-- MISSING, and why: (1) `entities` is always `[]`: the released seat sent every entity of a class the view packs declare (About:seat, fed by about.py with the
-- version, the git sha and the changelog); nothing here feeds those entities, and the engine's entities of those classes are not listed yet, so the About
-- window has nothing to draw; (2) the page's follow-up stream, `field.write` / `field.pack` / `field.remove` frames, is not on `/ui/serve/event` (it carries the
-- session events only), so the page's field never changes after the snapshot; (3) a Pack entity written by the model (`Pack:<name>.text`) is not in `packs`
-- (only files); (4) two folders holding the same pack name: either may win (the released seat had one folder).
-- (A VIRTUAL entity is collected when nothing holds it: `Boot:seat.fieldvm` holds `FieldVm:seat`, and its `dirs` and `files` getters hold the folders and files.)
-- The `packs` dict has data keys, which c1f cannot write: it is built by one `sql()` over the pairs (`json_group_object`, the way the session status is).

Boot.started on-setter fv-start:
  ALWAYS:
    ('FieldVm:seat').born = clock
    this.fieldvm = FieldVm:seat
    FOR d IN (this.app_dirs or []):
      ('FvDir:' + d).path = d

FvDir.entries getter: listdir(this.path)
FvDir.files getter: [[prop(e, 'name'), this.path + '/' + prop(e, 'name')] for e in this.entries if tail(prop(e, 'name'), 4) == '.c1f' and prop(e, 'kind') == 'file'] if this.entries != None else None

FvFile.text getter: read(this.path)
FvFile.stem getter: replace(this.file, '.c1f', '')
FvFile.view getter: '\nIMPORT dom ' in ('\n' + str(this.text or ''))

FieldVm.want getter: len(([b.app_dirs for b in instances('Boot') if b.app_dirs != None] or [[]])[0])
FieldVm.dirs getter: [d for d in instances('FvDir')]
-- each pack file of a folder is read by its own entity, born when the folder is listed (`opened` says it was)
FvDir.files on-setter fv-read:
  WHEN this.files != None:
    FOR r IN this.files:
      ('FvFile:' + r[1]).path = r[1]
      ('FvFile:' + r[1]).file = r[0]
    this.opened = True
FieldVm.listed getter: len(this.dirs) == this.want and len([d for d in this.dirs if d.opened != True]) == 0
FieldVm.files getter: [f for f in instances('FvFile')]
FieldVm.done getter: this.listed and len([f for f in this.files if f.text == None]) == 0
FieldVm.pairs getter: [[f.stem, f.text] for f in this.files if f.view]
FieldVm.rows getter: sql("SELECT json_group_object(json_extract(value, '$[0]'), json_extract(value, '$[1]')) AS packs FROM json_each(?)", this.pairs) if this.done else None
FieldVm.snapshot getter: {'packs': (json(prop(this.rows[0], 'packs')) or {}), 'entities': []} if (this.rows != None and len(this.rows) > 0) else None

Request.o_fieldvm getter: this.route == '/ui/fieldvm'
Request.m_fieldvm getter: ['GET']
Request.fv_seat getter: ([s for s in instances('FieldVm') if s.eid == 'FieldVm:seat'] or [None])[0]
Request.fv_body getter: this.fv_seat.snapshot if this.fv_seat != None else None
Request.r_fieldvm getter: {'status': 200, 'body': this.fv_body} if this.fv_body != None else None
